sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Client
    participant GW as API Gateway
    participant A as Authorizer Lambda
    participant B as Backend Lambda

    C->>GW: HTTPS request<br/>Authorization: Bearer eyJ…
    GW->>GW: TLS termination<br/>Route resolution

    Note over GW: Method has Lambda Authorizer attached

    GW->>A: invoke(event)<br/>{type: "TOKEN",<br/> authorizationToken,<br/> methodArn}
    activate A
    A->>A: validate token (iss, aud, exp, sig)
    A-->>GW: {principalId, policyDocument, context}
    deactivate A

    alt Effect: Allow
        GW->>B: invoke(integration)<br/>+ X-Amzn-Apigateway-Authorizer-* headers<br/>+ event.requestContext.authorizer
        activate B
        B-->>GW: 200 / 4xx / 5xx
        deactivate B
        GW-->>C: HTTP response
    else Effect: Deny
        GW-->>C: 403 Forbidden
    end

    Note over A,GW: For ReauthorizeEvery > 0, the Allow policy<br/>is cached per (methodArn) so subsequent<br/>requests within the TTL skip A entirely.
